From 45daf0b14d3de4e16cfb763714240cfa75855d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:44:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 56/58] feat(scripting): Mat4, Mat3 and a layer's
 getTransformMatrix

A layer's getTransformMatrix () returns its world transform as a Mat4,
and neither existed: a music widget reads which half of the screen it
sits in from m[12] and m[13], and its init threw before it set what the
rest of the widget reads.

Mat4 and Mat3 are the scene-script builtins' (JavaScript), with
Wallpaper Engine's whole API: identity, translation, scale, rotation
about an axis and from Euler angles, basis vectors, lookAt, compose and
decompose, add, subtract, multiply (by a matrix, a vector or a number),
translate, rotate, scale, transformPoint, transformDirection, transpose,
inverse, determinant, extractEuler, normalMatrix, copy, equals and
toString. `m` is column-major, as glm keeps it, so a Mat4's translation
is m[12], m[13] and m[14]. Angles are in degrees, Euler angles turn
about x, then y, then z, and a matrix without an inverse inverts to the
identity.

getTransformMatrix is the layer's origin, angle and scale with its
parents folded in, as the layer is drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
